; billboard -- VU1 microprogram, uploaded from VIDMABillboardMicrocode (0x004E5200).
; Generated by vudis.py extract; `vudis.py check` assembles it back
; against the SUPPORT image.  One line per instruction pair, upper first.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Uploaded by UploadBillboardMicro, which sets BASE 0x21A / OFFSET 0xF0 and
; MSCALFs VIBbRender (EndBillboards).  VIBbInit loads qwords 0..13 into
; vf01..vf14 (qword 12 into vf13.w only) and kicks the packet at 437, as the raster
; program's GIF area at 435 does.  VIBbRender is the DELAY SLOT of VIBbInit's
; [e]: the label is both.
;
; READ AND VERIFIED (spec_billboard.py; all 6 captured VIBbRender launches, 181
; billboards, 14 packets).  The data map (BeginBillboards, viraster.cpp):
;   0-3 model-view  4-7 projection->screen  8-11 model->clip  12 (1,1,1,1)
;   13 (offset x, offset y, 128, alpha scale 128 or 64)  16 the GIF tag
;   template (REGS RGBAQ ST XYZ2 XYZ2 ST XYZ2 ST XYZ2 ST XYZ2 XYZ2, PRE 0)
;   17-19 a PRE packet: PRIM 0x54 (strip, textured, blended, FLAT, no fog)
;   and one dummy vertex (512,512) -- so a batch is ONE triangle strip
;   32-59 the corner UVs of 7 sprite-sheet layouts (frame & 255 = 4*layout)
;   437 the material's layer-0 GS state, left there by the raster program
; Per billboard 11 qwords: RGBAQ, then (ST, XYZ2) for corners D A B C with D
; and C doubled (degenerate joins).  An off-screen billboard (any clip bit)
; is sent with zero size.  Packets ping-pong at 48 / 240 and are kicked at
; 16 billboards or at the frame's end mark (0x100, EndBillboards).
; THE UV TABLE OVERLAPS THE PACKET AT 48: layouts 4-6 read the packet being
; built (a rain splash in rain.bin does).

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

